@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/cka-theme.puml
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #326CE5
  ParticipantFontStyle bold
}
title From a Service name to a Pod

participant "front-end Pod" as p
participant "CoreDNS" as d
participant "Rules on this node\n(written by kube-proxy)" as r
participant "back-end Pod\n10.244.0.6:8080" as b

p -> d : what is back-end?
d --> p : A record: 10.106.127.123
p -> r : connect to 10.106.127.123:80
r -> r : match the Service, pick one endpoint,\nrewrite the destination
r -> b : 10.244.0.6:8080
b --> p : reply

caption <i>Two separate steps: DNS turns the name into the ClusterIP, then the node's rules turn the ClusterIP into a Pod.</i>\n<i>That is how to split a failure: if the name does not resolve, look at DNS; if the IP does not connect, look at endpoints and the rules.</i>
@enduml
